ps5: hdmi: undo the FLAVA3 "event 4" mute that blacks out the picture

Applies on top of linux.patch from ps5-linux-patches (tested on 1ec6a4a,
kernel 7.2.3) and 0002-ps5-hdmi-1440p120-and-sync-fixup.patch.
Apply with: patch -p1 < 0003-ps5-hdmi-event4-unmute.patch

About 1-3 s after a mode set, the FLAVA3 firmware sends HDMI event 4
(icc msg 0x8001, data[1] == 4), restarts HDCP on its own and mutes the
output. The picture goes black and the kernel logs nothing. Seen mostly
right after boot at 1440p120: the picture shows for a few seconds, then
goes black. Replugging the HDMI cable brings it back.

hdmi_notification_handler() now catches event 4, stops HDCP again and
unmutes video and audio, logging "event 4: stopped HDCP (r) and unmuted".
From ps5-linux-patches#55. Toggle: /sys/module/hdmi/parameters/event4_fix
(default Y; N only logs the event).

diff --git a/drivers/ps5/hdmi.c b/drivers/ps5/hdmi.c
index 2d8ed03..8268cec 100644
--- a/drivers/ps5/hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/ps5/hdmi.c
@@ -1416,8 +1416,30 @@ void hdmi_set_cec_handler(void (*handler)(void *data, const struct icc_msg *msg)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(hdmi_set_cec_handler);
 
+/*
+ * FLAVA3: ~1-3 s after a mode set the firmware sends HDMI event 4 and mutes
+ * the output (it restarts HDCP behind our back) -> black picture with no
+ * kernel error. Stop HDCP again and unmute (ps5-linux-patches#55).
+ * event4_fix=0 only logs the event.
+ */
+static bool event4_fix = true;
+module_param(event4_fix, bool, 0644);
+
 void hdmi_notification_handler(struct icc_msg *msg)
 {
+		if (msg->msg_type == 0x8001 && msg->data[1] == 0x04 &&
+		    hdmi_ic_type == HDMI_IC_TYPE_FLAVA3) {
+			if (event4_fix) {
+				int r = stopHdcpHw();
+
+				sceHdmiDeviceSetVideoMute(0);
+				sceHdmiSetAudioMute(0);
+				pr_info("event 4: stopped HDCP (%d) and unmuted\n", r);
+			} else {
+				pr_info("event 4 (event4_fix off)\n");
+			}
+		}
+
 		if (msg->data[1] == 0x02) {
 			fix_edid(&msg->data[4]);
 			real_edid = drm_edid_alloc(&msg->data[4], *(u16 *)&msg->data[2]);
